{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1792842979,"nonce":"tBCcTQfP/k38GzQWAjNFlboEdoc=","target":"584bd03c9904566130e0055bf841c711b12a9063b86f43dd0b8ea4d3403082f3","message":"- `FRESH_LOGIN_URL` (`lib.rs:1480`) and the CLI's `SETUP_LOGIN_PATH` (`scarab-cli/src/security.rs:25`) name no `provider`.\n- `oauth_provider(None)` answers 400 when several providers are configured and none is `unqualified_ids` (`lib.rs:622-647`). So \"Log in again\" and `scarab security setup` break on exactly that ADR-0069 configuration.\n- Fix: the CLI picks the provider through `/v1/auth/providers`, by the subject's prefix; the UI builds the href through `loginChoices`; or the server sends an ambiguous login that carries `next` to a UI chooser. Ticketed because it touches CLI, server and UI and is not cheap. It does not affect single-provider or default-provider installs.\n\nFound in the ADR-0073 step-up build review (AFK run 20261024-1301, review/judge.md T18); branch feat/step-up.","files":null}]}